.TH IOCTL 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
ioctl \- control a device
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <sys/ioctl.h>
.B int ioctl(int descriptor, unsigned long request, void* argument);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Passes a request and its argument to the Linux ioctl syscall. Unlike glibc's
variadic interface, Crunch requires all three arguments. Pass zero when no
argument is required; use ioctl_value for an integer argument.
The header defines FIONREAD, FIONBIO, FIOCLEX, FIONCLEX, TIOCGWINSZ,
TIOCSWINSZ and the Linux winsize structure. Consult the device's documentation
for the correct argument type and required storage.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the request\-specific result, or \-1 with errno set.
Success leaves errno unchanged.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ioctl (2)
